Current stage: Royal Assent (27 April 2026)
Stage history: Bill introduced 07 Jul 2025; Stage 1 09 Dec 2025; Stage 3 03 Mar 2026; Stage 3 29 Jan 2026; Stage 4 10 Mar 2026; Royal Assent 27 Apr 2026', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgIssueHistoryHome.aspx?IId=46141', '2026-04-27', '', '', '', '', '', 'Senedd', '', '', '', NULL, 130.0, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'building_safety_and_leasehold; named_welsh_legislation', 'Context; Property & energy', '', 'Bill progress', 'Building Safety (Wales) Act; Royal Assent; Stage 1; Stage 3; Stage 4; building safety', 0, '2026-08-04T14:04:20.996886', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgIssueHistoryHome.aspx?IId=46141', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('26ff52e60bb0fc04837b', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '10. Voting Time', 'Next, a vote on item 9, the debate on the first supplementary budget for 2026-27. I call for a vote on the motion, tabled in the name of Heledd Fychan. Open the vote. Close the vote. In favour 44, no abstentions and 49 against. The motion is therefore not agreed.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Huw Irranca-Davies', 'Llywydd', '5053', '', '', 'Plenary', '10. Voting Time', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=26577&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.868165', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767987', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('2762a6e874b06fbd99a3', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Social Justice', 'Thank you so much, Presiding Officer. Minister, fuel poverty has been, and remains, a huge concern for many residents across Wales, and it''s something my former colleague Mark Isherwood campaigned on tirelessly during his time here. We have heard warnings previously that the former Labour Government''s Warm Homes scheme was nowhere near what it needs to be and would not have provided what was required to tackle fuel poverty. A report by the Equality and Social Justice Committee back in 2025 found that it would take more than a century to improve the energy efficiency of all fuel-poor households.

 Cabinet Minister, Citizens Advice Cymru has reported that fuel debt is the No. 1 debt issue facing people using the charity''s services in many areas across Wales, including my own constituency of Newport and Islwyn. We know the Plaid Cymru Government has vowed in its first 100 days to plan to review the existing Warm Homes scheme, but many people, including my constituents, want and need action now. So, with the price cap having just increased, and no prediction for it to come down any time soon within the autumn, what support does the Welsh Government intend to provide people who will be experiencing fuel poverty? Thank you.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16084', '2026-07-08', 'Natasha Asghar', '', '336', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Social Justice', '16084', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16084?startPos=1542&l=en', NULL, 77.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'energy_efficiency', 'Property & energy', 'Sector bodies; First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Warm Homes; fuel poverty', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:15.596636', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16084&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#766828', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('2abf402a66205015a288', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', 'This is beneath you, finance Minister, it truly is. It truly is. And I wish that you would focus more on negotiations than attacks, I really do, because you may be more successful in getting future budgets through this Senedd.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Ken Skates', '', '267', '', '', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=26436&l=en', NULL, 44.0, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'Opposition housing leads', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.859541', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767977', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('2b8b8bf498c3f33ccc29', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Social Justice', 'Families across Wales are waiting to find out when exactly they will receive their child payments. The work needs to have been done with the DWP to make sure that it does fit with UK welfare benefits, and also with the use of data that can be done across with the UK Government. But it''s also critical that it''s done with local authorities on issues such as the council tax reduction scheme. So, can the Minister confirm when the child payments will start, and that it will not affect families'' eligibility for other financial support?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16084', '2026-07-08', 'Jayne Bryant', '', '5038', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the Deputy First Minister and Cabinet Minister for Social Justice', '16084', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16084?startPos=1024&l=en', NULL, 88.0, 'High', 'digest', 'taxation_of_property', 'Tax & finance', 'First Minister / Cabinet; Opposition housing leads', '', 'council tax; council tax reduction scheme', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:15.541377', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16084&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#766816', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('2efb9fc18f04bd7886bf', 'consultation', 'Senedd — Committee work', 'Forward work programme – Legislation Committee', 'Forward work programme – Legislation Committee

Forward work programme – Legislation Committee Forward work programme – Legislation Committee Issue Details Issue History Related Meetings The forward work programme of the Legislation Committee sets out the work which the Committee is intending to carry out in the following weeks and months. The Legislation Committee''s forward work programme is often determined by its responsibilities set out in Standing Orders 21 and 21C. On a routine basis, the Committee considers subordinate legislation and legislative consent memoranda which are laid before the Senedd. For further details, please see the ''Current Work'' information on the Committee''s homepage. Any documents published indicate the current intentions of the Committee at the time of publishing, however the programme may change at any time to respond to external events. Business type: Other First published: 11/06/2026 Topics Helpful Links Find a Member of the Senedd chevron_right Sign up to updates from Senedd committees chevron_right Senedd Now chevron_right Glossary chevron_right Related No results were found', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgIssueHistoryHome.aspx?IId=47572', '2026-08-04', '', '', '', '', '', 'Legislation Committee', '', '', '', NULL, 140.0, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Legislative commitment; Bill progress', 'Legislation Committee; laid before the Senedd; subordinate legislation', 0, '2026-08-04T14:02:50.494140', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgIssueHistoryHome.aspx?IId=47572', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('2f8aebbd596da95efef1', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', 'You took a couple of interventions.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Huw Irranca-Davies', '', '5053', '', '', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=26312&l=en', NULL, 16.5, 'Noise', 'archive', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', '', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.845871', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#768002', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('30f3da5e650a788c6444', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '6. Member Debate under Standing Order 11.21(iv): Young people and employment', 'I''m pleased to support this motion today, and I thank Shav Taj for giving me the opportunity to speak about it. At its heart, this motion is about a simple principle: every young person in our nation deserves the opportunity to build a secure, sustainable and rewarding future here in Wales. The Well-being of Future Generations (Wales) Act 2015 calls on us to think about the long term. That means ensuring young people are not simply finding jobs, but building careers that are sustainable, resilient and futureproof.

 Much can be said about the barriers facing young people, from low pay and insecure work to a lack of progression opportunities, but I want to focus on the opportunities being created by our climate commitments, and the good-quality jobs that can come with them. As Greens, we see meeting our climate commitments not as a burden, but as a huge opportunity. It can create thousands of long-term skilled jobs. Crucially, we need careers that equip young people with skills for life. We should not be directing people into industries with an expiry date attached to them. Instead, we should be investing in sectors that we know will continue to grow and provide stable employment for decades to come.

 Some of those careers will be in the trades. We need to deliver renewable energy projects, retrofit our existing housing stock and build the sustainable homes and infrastructure of the future. We need more engineers, more skilled construction workers and more investment in research and development if Wales is to become that global leader.

 I''d like to highlight the potential of marine and tidal energy. Wales is blessed with extraordinary coastlines and the second largest tidal range in the world. By harnessing that natural advantage, we can create skilled careers by strengthening our energy security. If Wales isn''t ready for this transition, it''s our young people who will, once again, miss the boat. We need to be able to equip them to move into these good long-term careers, otherwise the opportunities will simply go elsewhere.

 The Warm Homes plan is another good example of where environmental and economic goals come together. Retrofitting homes and building fossil-fuel-free homes from the outset will cut emissions, lower energy bills and create skilled employment in construction and engineering. These are jobs rooted in communities, and jobs that we will need if we are serious about meeting our climate commitments. That''s why I''m so pleased to support this motion, and I urge the Welsh Government to consider and ensure that the pathways into green industries are ambitious, accessible and available to young people across Wales. Diolch.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16086', '2026-07-15', 'Paul Rock', '', '12176', '', '', 'Plenary', '6. Member Debate under Standing Order 11.21(iv): Young people and employment', '16086', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16086?startPos=9326&l=en', NULL, 71.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'energy_efficiency', 'Property & energy', 'LGHP Committee members', '', 'Warm Homes; retrofit; retrofitting', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:05.605230', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16086&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#768277', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('326fbdba7770cc10b499', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning', 'Thank you very much. There are a number of reasons why it''s important that we improve the standard of our housing. One is to decarbonise so that we in Wales contribute less to climate change through our housing sector. Housing contributes around 11 per cent of carbon emissions in Wales, and I am very eager to see that reduced, and having a plan to decarbonise homes is very important. But there are benefits in terms of reducing bills as a result of making our homes more energy efficient—it''s important that we consider that—and fuel poverty is also an issue in Wales, and it''ll help us tackle poverty more generally. But also there is the impact on health, which is crucially important, and I am having discussions with the Deputy Minister in relation to preventative work, because, for me, housing is central to improving people''s health, and we can improve health outcomes for our nation by having a clear focus on improving our housing standards. I will be going on Thursday to see—it''s social housing—how retrofit programmes have helped a particular family there, and I''ll be making further announcements on this specific area in our first 100 days.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16086', '2026-07-15', 'Sian Gwenllian', '', '4981', '', '', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning', '16086', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16086?startPos=5857&l=en', NULL, 126.5, 'High', 'digest', 'hmos_and_standards; energy_efficiency; social_housing', 'Housing system; Private rented sector; Property & energy', 'Housing minister', '', 'decarbonise homes; fuel poverty; housing standards; retrofit; social housing', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:05.262254', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16086&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#768206', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('32a139fa967a5f41c133', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', 'Huw, my apologies. My apologies. It is sometimes challenging to hear contributions in the Chamber. Please if you can keep the noise down so we can hear.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Huw Irranca-Davies', 'Llywydd', '5053', '', '', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=24190&l=en', NULL, 16.5, 'Noise', 'archive', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', '', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.610861', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767894', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('33489ff1bf05a188d799', 'oral_question', 'Question not reached in Plenary', 'Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning', '<p>Adequate and efficient infrastructure, including services such as education and health, is crucial for economic, social and environmental sustainability. Planning authorities should, in conjunction with key providers, take a strategic and long-term approach towards the provision of infrastructure as part of local plan development.</p>', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16086', '2026-07-15', '', 'Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning', '', '', '', 'Plenary', 'Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning', '16086', '', NULL, 55.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'planning_system', 'Planning & place', 'Housing minister', '', 'planning authorities', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:07.001429', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16086&xmlDownloadType=QNR', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('33d24252f0fd0505cb76', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', 'I thank the spokesperson for those comments. I can count, thank you very much; one of my favourite things to do is counting and adding up data. We have clear plans in place for our expenditure. I very much hope that there will be cross-Senedd support for the supplementary budget, which reflects the priorities that the people of Wales voted for in the election. I hope that colleagues across this Senedd will work to ensure that the Welsh Government and the public sector in Wales work at their most effective and that we, over the next four years, can identify more funding that can be invested in the priorities of the people, to support childcare, to support the economy, to support the health service.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Dafydd Trystan Davies', '', '12140', '', '', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=4112&l=en', NULL, 16.5, 'Noise', 'archive', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', '', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:08.563485', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767608', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('341afd3b54bce0d36c8f', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', 'To Labour Members, old and new, I know that you have recently been badly defeated in an election. I know it''s painful and confusing. I have been there. But, ultimately, you will not be defined by that loss, but how you respond to it. It can make a party or break it. You''ve been lately quite keen, in this Chamber, to point us in Plaid Cymru to Scotland. Well, I point you to Scotland, too. Look at your sister party in permanent opposition since 2007. Today, you will not only vote against the retention, intact, of your own Welsh Labour Government budget, but also against new money to reduce NHS waiting lists, to provide more free childcare, to extend £1 bus travel for young people, to spend more on backlog maintenance for schools and hospitals.

 Last week, Labour, you voted with Reform to ensure that this Senedd voted against fair funding for Wales. Labour voted against fair funding for Wales. I shudder to think how successive successful previous Labour First Ministers would have viewed that. Today, you vote against £120 million for ALN provision in Wales, with Reform. You will be voting with parties of the right, who will welcome you. [ Interruption .] Hear them. Hear them. They will welcome you with open arms, because you will give them their majority today. And you are doing so against a progressive budget that provides more support for those most in need in Wales.

 The fine statue of Rhodri Morgan is tonight watching its first vote in this Senedd since it was unveiled. I served as a Minister in his Government. He reflected the progressive co-operative values of the Labour Party in Wales. Today, Labour have abandoned those values. And in these final few moments before the vote, there is still time for you to reclaim them. Reclaim them.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Elin Jones', '', '162', '', '', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=26318&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.849227', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#768005', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('34a009e32b296b4ebb1e', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', 'I mean, the costings around the childcare offer have been made public, and they are very much a part of the supplementary budget that is due to be voted on today. The childcare offer is made up of a specific fund of £55 million that is going to be partly in capital, partly in resource, to make sure that we''re able to deliver, as the first phase of the roll-out of costed childcare, the completion of the 12.5 hours for two-year-olds. Now, that is what is being done. I literally cannot give you more detail than that. It''s the money, it''s the timescale, and it''s going to be done within this financial year.

 Now, I know the Member couldn''t decide which question to ask today, so he tried to bring eight into one. But in terms of accusing me of giving an off-the-cuff reply on the M4, it was an off-the-cuff reply based on 15 years of Plaid Cymru policy that we want to see a solution to the problems on the M4 in the Newport area—work that has already begun under my Deputy Minister for Transport and that we will be reporting on in the autumn of this year.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Rhun ap Iorwerth', 'First Minister of Wales', '2717', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=1045&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:08.277585', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767480', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('35220740d2a8da222e4f', 'consultation', 'Senedd — Committee work', 'Forward work programme – Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', 'Forward work programme – Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee

Forward work programme – Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee Forward work programme – Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee Consultation: Priorities for the Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee Issue Details Issue History Related Meetings The forward work programme of the Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee sets out the work which the Committee is intending to carry out in the following weeks and months. Any documents published indicate the current intentions of the Committee at the time of publishing, however the programme may change at any time to respond to external events. ¬¬¬ Consultation: Priorities for the Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee The Committee is seeking views from people and organisations on the issues they believe it should prioritise in the Seventh Senedd. Further information on how to submit your views is available on the consultation page . zzz Business type: Other First published: 15/06/2026 Consultations Priorities for the Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee (running until 11/09/2026) Topics Helpful Links Find a Member of the Senedd chevron_right Sign up to updates from Senedd committees chevron_right Senedd Now chevron_right Glossary chevron_right Related No results were found', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgIssueHistoryHome.aspx?IId=47576', '2026-08-04', '', '', '', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '', '', '', NULL, 98.0, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Consultation open', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee; consultation; consultations; seeking views', 0, '2026-08-04T14:02:45.848130', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgIssueHistoryHome.aspx?IId=47576', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('36a638eb6e90f5dd172e', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', 'Of course, my Government will do everything we can and already have done to support those who are affected by these fires. My thanks initially go to the people who responded to them. My thoughts are with the people who are affected by them.

 On the question of a Minister for north Wales, I have a Minister for north Wales. It''s Siân Gwenllian, and it''s Dafydd Trystan, and it''s Anna Brychan, it''s Mabon ap Gwynfor, it''s Sioned Williams—all my Ministers are Ministers for all of Wales. Where was Labour''s Minister for the south of Wales, if that matters? Because all my Ministers are Ministers for the south of Wales too, and the west of Wales, and mid Wales, because we are a joined-up Government that has a plan for our nation—all of our nation.

 That is why all of us have come together around this supplementary budget today—north, south, east, west, and mid, it''s important to remember—with a determination to change the lives of the people of Wales for the better. We have a supplementary budget that is focused on making the NHS sustainable. I will be voting for that sustainability for the NHS. The leader of Labour in Wales is threatening to vote against that. I will be voting for expanding free school meals under this supplementary budget. The Labour leader here is threatening to vote against that. I will be voting for the expansion of paid-for childcare in Wales. The Labour leader threatens to vote against that. And, yes, I will be voting for a package worth £120 million for ALN that he and I negotiated positively on, and he is threatening to vote to not allow that spending to go ahead. This is a Government for all of Wales with a vision for all of our nation.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Rhun ap Iorwerth', 'First Minister of Wales', '2717', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=1314&l=en', NULL, 71.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'Housing minister; First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:08.311408', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767509', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
