This is an opportunity to influence: committee papers and any call for written evidence are normally published in the two weeks beforehand.', 'https://business.senedd.wales/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=986&MId=16254', '2026-09-21', '', '', '', '', '', 'Legislation Committee', '', '16254', '', '2026-09-21', 48.0, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Legislation Committee; written evidence', 0, '2026-08-04T14:04:40.425615', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgWebService.asmx#GetAllMeetingsByDate', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('3a6d8aa0f9d0ea87d273', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '6. Statement by the Deputy Minister for Public and Preventative Health: Priorities for Public and Preventative Health', 'Well, I''m glad you agree with the priority that we''ve put on tackling waiting lists and the investment that we''ve set out in the supplementary budget in order to do that. I hope, indeed, that Members would reflect on what voting against that supplementary budget would mean in terms of the investment that we need in our NHS and across other preventative health measures. There''s investment in the supplementary budget on the swimming initiative for schools as well. So, voting against the supplementary budget this afternoon does have serious consequences in terms of the ability of our NHS to respond to the demands it''s facing now and the backlog that we have inherited from the previous Government, which absolutely impacts on the issues that you mentioned about the provision of health services in our rural communities. I am also from rural west Wales and know the challenges. As the First Minister set out earlier this afternoon, our ambition is to make sure that we look at rural-proofing, to make sure that the cost of delivery of services really does adequately reflect the actual costs in terms of what''s being funded, and that is a key central part. But I''d urge Members across this Chamber to make sure that they support the supplementary budget, to make sure of exactly what you mentioned, in terms of tackling the waiting lists and making sure our health and social care system is on a sustainable footing.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Nerys Evans', '', '261', '', '', 'Plenary', '6. Statement by the Deputy Minister for Public and Preventative Health: Priorities for Public and Preventative Health', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=16878&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:09.918256', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767878', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('3a7e5e3dfa307c0b54d9', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', 'As such, I will helpfully remind Members if they exceed the time. I ask Members to work with me; there are a lot of speakers down for this debate.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Huw Irranca-Davies', 'Llywydd', '5053', '', '', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=23410&l=en', NULL, 16.5, 'Noise', 'archive', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', '', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.523612', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767984', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('3d22ca7f988f94317b91', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', 'But you are rejecting the deal that would have secured £120 million additional spending on additional learning needs, as you brought to the table. So, I remain, despite that contribution, totally flabbergasted.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Elin Jones', '', '162', '', '', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=26155&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.824139', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767994', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('3d7021da1680eecc01f5', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', 'Fifteen years, and all your transport Minister could come up with is closing junctions. Now, one way to stop congestion is to stop cars getting onto the M4. I''ll give you that, but the people of Newport will not be very happy with that.

 I asked for initial costings. Costings for phase 1 is not the initial costings. You said during the election campaign your promises were fully costed. Then you''re downgrading them to initial costings. Then you''re downgrading it to costings for phase 1. So, you clearly haven''t got a plan. And if we do get those costings within the first 100 days, the 100 days ends during recess. So, we can''t scrutinise when you actually issue those, but we will be here in September, waiting to scrutinise those figures.

 But, First Minister, if your supplementary budget is voted down today, are you prepared to come back during the summer recess with a revised budget, or is this a part-time Plaid Government? Or are you content for the plans within your supplementary budget to languish for months upon months because you''re too stubborn to do a deal?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Dan Thomas', '', '12147', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=1112&l=en', NULL, 66.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet; Opposition housing leads', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:08.287615', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767490', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('3dd0b0bbccd2321fed46', 'calendar', 'Senedd forward look', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee — 16 September 2026, 09.30', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee is scheduled to meet on 16 September 2026 at 09.30.
Meeting status: Confirmed
This is an opportunity to influence: committee papers and any call for written evidence are normally published in the two weeks beforehand.', 'https://business.senedd.wales/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=983&MId=16246', '2026-09-16', '', '', '', '', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '', '16246', '', '2026-09-16', 48.0, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee; written evidence', 0, '2026-08-04T14:04:40.405241', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgWebService.asmx#GetAllMeetingsByDate', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('3eb97b46f43c0a339f2e', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning', 'Thank you for the question, and I''m pleased that we do agree that we need to look seriously at ''Future Wales'', namely the national plan, the top-tier plan on developments in Wales. It''s under that, of course, that ''Planning Policy Wales'' lies. So, we need to do the work on that highest level around the national spatial strategy and to include in that the current priorities for growth, infrastructure and regional development and transport. So, it does have statutory status, and I''m very eager, as the work has started to look at that highest level, to then see what needs to be changed in terms of the planning policies, including energy policy, electrification and new electrical lines, and so forth. So, I can assure you that that work is happening.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16086', '2026-07-15', 'Sian Gwenllian', '', '4981', '', '', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning', '16086', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16086?startPos=4926&l=en', NULL, 60.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'planning_system', 'Planning & place', 'Housing minister', '', 'Future Wales; Planning Policy Wales; planning policy', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:05.168591', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16086&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#768159', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('3f383329b1d810d24f20', 'committee_transcript', 'Petitions Committee', '2. Updates - Petitions referred to the Seventh Senedd', 'Thank you very much, Chair. This petition was discussed in the last meeting of the previous Petitions Committee. I noted that Joel James MS had said he would leave us a prod for us to consider it in this Senedd term—so he can consider us successfully prodded to do so.

 It touches on an issue that the previous committee had considered with a few different landfill sites, but this one in particular has been ongoing for a number of years. Our predecessor committee felt that there was still a lot to be done on this particular petition, even though they''d had a response from the former Deputy First Minister, whose portfolio this fell into. Our predecessor committee agreed to refer it on to us, with a view that we might perhaps like to highlight it with the relevant policy committee and pursue the appropriate Minister with responsibility for landfill operations on all these issues around forever chemicals, water quality and odours.

 So, I think there''s one course of action that I would like to suggest for us, which is to take it up, first of all, with the new Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee. We could ask them to pursue the matters raised by the petition with the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability, and I think it would be appropriate for us to do that because I know that committee is looking to bring that Minister in for general scrutiny as soon as possible. That committee is also looking at its forward work plans, so all of these issues around landfill, water pollution and the air quality issues could be something that the committee might wish to consider more broadly, as well as taking up directly with the Minister.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16175', '2026-07-09', 'Vikki Howells', '', '5107', '', '', 'Petitions Committee', '2. Updates - Petitions referred to the Seventh Senedd', '16175', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16175?startPos=801&l=en', NULL, 57.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:13.263366', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16175&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767266', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('3f48ebf29c69963ceb8b', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning', 'Thank you very much. To return to your point on the Cladiators, yes, I had a very constructive meeting with them on Monday. I was delighted to meet with them and to hear their concerns directly from them.

 I made a written statement on Monday that confirmed the 20,000 social homes that are desperately needed in Wales, for everyone living in Wales. The way that social housing is allocated is a matter for local authorities. Local authorities have a housing register and homes are allocated according to need, and that''s how it should be too. Therefore, I look forward to the work now of supplying more social homes. That''s what''s at the heart of the problem; the core of the housing crisis in Wales is that we don''t have enough social homes. The supply isn''t adequate to meet demand, and that is where we should be focusing our efforts always.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16086', '2026-07-15', 'Sian Gwenllian', '', '4981', '', '', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning', '16086', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16086?startPos=4017&l=en', NULL, 93.5, 'High', 'digest', 'housing_supply; social_housing', 'Housing system; Planning & place', 'Sector bodies; Housing minister', '', 'social homes; social housing', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:05.069546', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16086&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#768148', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('40665fa746a8cc7a5386', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', 'I agree with your last point, Darren. What I don''t agree with is describing Plaid Cymru as a left-wing party.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Mike Hedges', '', '332', '', '', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=24343&l=en', NULL, 44.0, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'Opposition housing leads', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.628722', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#767895', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('40e092e444c120b3c4a3', 'legislation', 'Acts of Senedd Cymru', 'Visitor Accommodation (Register and Levy) Etc. (Wales) Act 2025', 'Visitor Accommodation (Register and Levy) Etc. (Wales) Act 2025', 'https://www.legislation.gov.uk/asc/2025/5/2025-09-19/data.xml', '2026-05-06', '', '', '', '', '', 'legislation.gov.uk', '', '', '', NULL, 84.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'second_homes_and_short_term_lets; named_welsh_legislation', 'Context; Planning & place', '', '', 'Visitor Accommodation (Register and Levy); visitor accommodation', 0, '2026-08-04T14:04:14.614021', 'https://www.legislation.gov.uk/asc/data.feed', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
