Forward work programme – Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee Forward work programme – Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee Consultation: Priorities Consultation: Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee Issue Details Related Meetings The forward work programme of the Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee sets out the work which the Committee is intending to carry out in the following weeks and months. Any documents published indicate the current intentions of the Committee at the time of publishing, however the programme may change at any time to respond to external events. Type: For information First published: 15/06/2026 Consultations Priorities Consultation: Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee (running until 18/09/2026) Topics Helpful Links Find a Member of the Senedd chevron_right Sign up to updates from Senedd committees chevron_right Senedd Now chevron_right Glossary chevron_right Related No results were found', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgIssueHistoryHome.aspx?IId=47634', '2026-08-04', '', '', '', '', '', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee', '', '', '', NULL, 98.0, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Consultation open', 'Equality, Human Rights and Social Justice Committee; consultation; consultations', 0, '2026-08-04T14:02:47.583055', 'https://business.senedd.wales/mgIssueHistoryHome.aspx?IId=47634', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO items (uid, source_kind, source_name, title, body, url, item_date, speaker, speaker_role, speaker_id, party, constituency, forum, agenda_item, meeting_id, video_url, deadline, score, band, channel, themes, tiers, entities, signals, matched_terms, force_alert, collected_at, raw_ref, notified_at, reviewed_by, review_note, review_status) VALUES ('dca838f7a61550b2ab2c', 'plenary_transcript', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', 'Thank you for that. You''re absolutely right, there is a responsibility on all of us to consider the multifaceted impacts that this kind of large infrastructure has. The environmental one is one in particular. You may be aware, of course, that planning policy reform, hopefully, is on its way, where the Government will be reviewing and updating national planning policy so that we can better enable some of these decisions to be done in a way that aligns all of these considerations that need to be taken on board when it comes to energy policy, the planning system, clearer spatial guidance, the environmental impact as well. So, it''s work in progress. It''s something we''re very mindful of and something we''re serious about addressing.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16084', '2026-07-08', 'Llyr Gruffydd', '', '425', '', '', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', '16084', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16084?startPos=3470&l=en', NULL, 27.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'planning_system', 'Planning & place', '', '', 'planning policy; planning system', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:15.780720', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16084&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#766900', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
